    <summary>SMCIPMITool is Supermicro's out-of-band command line utility for managing IPMI devices (BMC) and SuperBlade systems over the network.</summary>
    <description>SMCIPMITool is a command line interface utility for Supermicro IPMI devices (BMC) and SuperBlade systems. It manages servers out-of-band, over the network, and complements the in-band IPMICFG.

Key features:

  - IPMI and Supermicro OEM commands against a remote BMC (power control, sensors, SEL, FRU, users, network settings)
  - BMC and BIOS firmware update, virtual media and remote KVM launch
  - SuperBlade, MicroBlade and other chassis management
  - Shell mode and batch execution across many hosts

The package ships the official Windows build with its bundled Java runtime (no Java installation needed). Only `smcipmitool` is put on the PATH: the bundled `java.exe` and the other runtime tools are not shimmed.</description>
    <releaseNotes>## SMCIPMITool 2.30.0 (build 250915)

Released 2025-09-15 (build date).
- Embeds the official archive from Supermicro's download center
  (`https://www.supermicro.com/Bios/sw_download/993/SMCIPMITool_2.30.0_build.250915_bundleJRE_Windows.zip`), redistributed with Supermicro's permission — nothing is downloaded at install time;
  see legal\VERIFICATION.txt.
- sha256 `FE3D2B9AA4A8B070529D92DE4DB4D0B56E0978A66C66EB405F19B6E1F43F3A74`.
- Portable: extracted into the package folder; the command is `smcipmitool`.
- The bundled JRE is used, so no Java installation is needed; its executables are not shimmed.
    </releaseNotes>
